<title>ITALY: Agip, Shell to invest $50 mln in Falklands.</title>
<headline>Agip, Shell to invest $50 mln in Falklands.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agip, the exploration and production arm of Italy's energy giant ENI, said on Monday that it had won a bid with Shell to explore for oil off the Falkland Islands in the South Atlantic.</p>
<p>Agip said in a statement that the exploration zone covered 1,621 square km in a area some 200 km north of the Falklands.</p>
<p>It said that Agip would have a 30 percent stake in the joint venture while Shell would have 70 percent stake. The investment for the two exploratory wells was valued at $50 million.</p>
<p>The work, set to start in 1997, would be carried out by Shell Exploration B.V.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +00396 6782501</p>
</text>
